  "raw_text": "Step 1: We use polynomial long division to divide \\(x^6 - 3\\) by \\(x + 1\\).\n\nStep 2: Set up the division with \\(x^6 - 3\\) under the division symbol and \\(x + 1\\) outside.\n\nStep 3: Divide the leading term of the dividend \\(x^6\\) by the leading term of the divisor \\(x\\), which gives \\(x^5\\). Write \\(x^5\\) above the division symbol.\n\nStep 4: Multiply \\(x^5\\) by \\(x + 1\\) to get \\(x^6 + x^5\\). Subtract this from \\(x^6 - 3\\) to get \\(-x^5 - 3\\).\n\nStep 5: Bring down the next term (which is 0 since there is no \\(x^5\\) term in the original polynomial) to get \\(-x^5 - 3\\).\n\nStep 6: Repeat the process by dividing \\(-x^5\\) by \\(x\\) to get \\(-x^4\\). Write \\(-x^4\\) above the division symbol.\n\nStep 7: Multiply \\(-x^4\\) by \\(x + 1\\) to get \\(-x^5 - x^4\\). Subtract this from \\(-x^5 - 3\\) to get \\(x^4 - 3\\).\n\nStep 8: Continue this process until all terms are divided. The next steps will be:\n\n- Divide \\(x^4\\) by \\(x\\) to get \\(x^3\\).\n- Multiply \\(x^3\\) by \\(x + 1\\) to get \\(x^4 + x^3\\).\n- Subtract to get \\(-x^3 - 3\\).\n\n- Divide \\(-x^3\\) by \\(x\\) to get \\(-x^2\\).\n- Multiply \\(-x^2\\) by \\(x + 1\\) to get \\(-x^3 - x^2\\).\n- Subtract to get \\(x^2 - 3\\).\n\n- Divide \\(x^2\\) by \\(x\\) to get \\(x\\).\n- Multiply \\(x\\) by \\(x + 1\\) to get \\(x^2 + x\\).\n- Subtract to get \\(-x - 3\\).\n\n- Divide \\(-x\\) by \\(x\\) to get \\(-1\\).\n- Multiply \\(-1\\) by \\(x + 1\\) to get \\(-x - 1\\).\n- Subtract to get \\(-2\\).\n\nStep 9: The quotient is \\(x^5 - x^4 + x^3 - x^2 + x - 1\\) and the remainder is \\(-2\\).\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{x^5 - x^4 + x^3 - x^2 + x - 1}<|im_end|>",
